  "query_preview": "..\nSome brief thunderstorms were visible today as moderate wind shear \nand weak upper level support developed over the convergence zone.\nThis is moving out of the region so thunderstorms are no longer\nexpected for the islands but may be visible off the coast tonight.\nOtherwise, showers are expected to remain isolated at least the next\nfew days with occasional patches of weak, scattered trade wind \nshowers possible. Gentle winds tonight will become gentle to moderate\ntomorrow and may increase slightly by the end of the week. Models \nindicate a trade wind trough may move into or just north of the \nMarianas by Friday, possibly bringing more rainfall. However, the \nlocation of this trough remains uncertain so isolated showers remain \nin the forecast.",
